WEBVTT

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.020
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.130
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.970
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.640
<i>This day has come again this year.</i>

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:20.650
<i>The roots of the blood that flows
in my body and my flesh and soul.</i>

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.980
<i>A place I'm connected with by destiny...</i>

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.650
<i>This craft will be landing shortly.</i>

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.660
<i>Please fasten your seatbelts
securely around your waists.</i>

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.830
<i>It's summer again.
Once again this day has come.</i>

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:50.840
YONAGO AIRPORT TERMINAL

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:50.840
<i>The day I visit my dad's hometown,
the town of Sakaiminato that I love!</i>

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.930
CHAPTER 16

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.850
THE MYSTERY OF THE TIDE! UMIZATO

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.730
SAKAIMINATO STATION

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.980
I made it!

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.350
Mana!

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.900
Uncle Shoji! Aunt Rie!

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:09.150
Welcome, Mana-chan.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.870
If you'd called us when your plane left
we'd have picked you up at the airport.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.580
Good for you,
not getting lost on your own.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.080
I'm not a kid anymore!

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.670
We're glad you came so far to this place.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:29.210
I've made lots of
the minced sardine soup you love so much.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:33.260
I thought you would,
so I made sure to be extra hungry!

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:34.220
Oh my!

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:36.720
That's my niece for you.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:40.270
I hear Yuichi-san had
some last-minute work?

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:42.390
He said he'll come once he's done.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.560
Mom said she couldn't
leave Dad alone either.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.150
But I just couldn't wait!

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.530
Let's eat!

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:54.990
<i>A hit!</i>

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.200
More please!

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:57.030
Okay.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.410
Like father, like daughter.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:04.420
Yuichi loved the minced sardine soup
that Mom used to make, too.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.880
<i>Safe! Safe!</i>

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.380
<i>Two to one! Tottori Academy
has let Kanagawa East take the lead!</i>

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:15.840
Dammit! What are they doing?

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.310
I could have made that throw in time!

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:23.310
That's right! When you played in the
Koshien series, you played center, right?

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:28.190
Yup! The club members
used to call me Sniper Shoji!

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:34.360
SAKAIMINATO HIGH
FAILS TO MAKE THE FINALS!

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.780
We barely had nine members.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.360
I had to beg a friend
to be the team manager.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:38.080
The reason our weak team
was able to beat other tough teams...

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:41.080
Well, it was thanks to
this powerful shoulder!

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.580
That's enough already.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:48.040
You brag about that every year.
We're getting blisters on our ears, right?

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:52.840
Nah, I love hearing Uncle Shoji's
Koshien series stories.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:55.510
It makes me feel like
summer's really here.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.800
That and the Harbor Fishing Festival!

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:04.690
I love that feverish excitement when
everybody in Sakaiminato gets together!

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:06.440
It starts this week, right?

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.360
Will there be
lots of people again this year?

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:13.990
What's wrong?

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:16.490
Actually, Mana-chan...

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.450
Huh?

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:21.740
SAKAIMINATO CITY HALL

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:25.540
Between the people living in Sakaiminato,
and those who have come back from the city

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:29.880
73RD HARBOR FISHING FESTIVAL
PREPARATION COMMITTEE

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:29.880
along with the people who
have recently moved to Sakaiminato...

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:34.460
There was a divide between
how to hold the festival.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:38.470
The town of Sakaiminato is
split in two right now.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:41.850
If you fear change,
you'll drive people away!

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.350
What kind of festival has no people?!

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:46.690
A festival should be more dignified!

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:49.520
We have to protect what needs protecting!

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.520
Normally in summer,

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:56.780
the town would be full of lanterns
of all shapes and sizes by now.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:02.530
Everybody wants what they think is best
for the festival, so it's difficult.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.660
Are they even going to do
the festival this year?

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.290
I was really looking forward to it...

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:13.960
She seems really disappointed.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.670
I wish there was a way
we could cheer her up.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.930
It's been a while. Maybe I'll go fishing
on Kinopee's boat tomorrow.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:26.730
At least we can feed her
the liveliest fish I can catch.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:32.690
Oh, so Mana's at her father's hometown.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:35.690
It sounds like she was
really looking forward to it.

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:40.910
Since before summer break she was saying
"I can't wait to go to Sakaiminato."

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.240
Sakaiminato?

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:45.740
What?

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.870
Well, come to think of it,
the other day Rat Man was saying

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:57.010
there's something profitable
and invited me to Sakaiminato with him.

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:01.220
From what I heard,

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:06.890
cargo ships called <i>kitamaebune</i>
sank with tons of treasure inside.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:10.440
What's more, some are
still at the bottom of the ocean?

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:14.480
Could they be waiting for me to
pull them up?

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:16.400
Here we go.

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:25.620
Treasure-chan!
Where, where, where? Where are you?

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.250
Treasure already?!

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:47.680
If you're empty then don't have
such a big conspicuous lid, dammit!

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:58.730
Okay! Start getting the nets ready!

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.280
Okay!

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.450
Huh?

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.200
What's that sound?

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.290
Isn't it a <i>biwa</i>?

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:14.210
A <i>biwa</i>? One of those shamisen-like things?

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:17.590
What would it be doing in
the middle of a fishing spot?

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:18.920
What the...?!

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:21.760
What is it, Kinopee?

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.510
Th-That!

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:39.190
Where are you, mountains of treasure-chan?

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:42.690
A small shrine?
Why's it at the bottom of the ocean...?

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.860
Maybe in there?

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.490
It won't budge...

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:52.500
That makes me more curious
about what's inside.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:54.500
Huh?

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.710
Fish? No, turtles?

00:08:58.590 --> 00:08:59.630
Huh?

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:10.560
Whoa, whoa, whoa, seriously?

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:16.650
-They're late.
-This has never happened before.

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:21.230
I know. The boat
should have been back long ago.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.990
They're sending what boats they can
to search.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:26.950
Did something happen to Uncle
and the others?

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:33.830
Okay, the Ebisumaru goes west,
the Daikokumaru goes north!

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:36.670
My boat will search the southern area!

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.540
The Fukujinmaru takes the east!

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:39.670
Okay!

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.170
It's all right.

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:47.340
You don't have to worry, Mana-chan.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:55.180
Mana-chan?!

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:57.980
Hey!

00:09:58.560 --> 00:09:59.980
Mana-chan!

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:02.730
I'll search, too!

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.360
I can't just sit around!

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:09.490
Uncle!

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.620
Uncle Shoji!

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:14.120
Dammit, a fog's rolling in.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.000
We can't search like this.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:18.710
Uncle Shoji!

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:24.880
Give me a ladle...

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:27.970
-Give me a ladle...
-What's that voice?

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:31.470
Give me a ladle...

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:35.060
Give me a ladle...

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:38.810
Give me a ladle...

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.730
Give me a ladle...

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:46.320
Give me a ladle...

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:50.360
Give me a ladle...

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:53.910
Give me a ladle...

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:56.120
I-I-Is that what you want?!

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:17.560
What is this?!

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:44.130
Let go!

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:45.880
No!

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:54.970
Run...

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:05.980
<i>YOKAI</i> UMIZATO

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:10.570
MIZUKI SHIGERU MEMORIAL MUSEUM
(SAKAIMINATO CITY)

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:09.570
<i>-"Oh no..."
-"I'll turn this into money."</i>

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:10.570
<i>"Smack!"</i>

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:14.870
Mana-chan? Mana-chan!

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:20.910
Aunt...?

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:24.710
Where am I?

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:26.250
It's Yumigahama.

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:32.090
Where's everyone?!

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:34.590
You're the only one who washed up.

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:36.550
What happened?

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:39.350
<i>Yokai</i>?!

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:40.600
Yeah.

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:43.100
But why was I the only one...?

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:50.400
Uncle Shoji's baseball...?

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:55.610
That <i>yokai</i> was Uncle Shoji?!

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:03.040
Hmm. Those must be Funa-Yurei.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.750
Boat ghosts?

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:11.510
It's said they sink boats with ladles
and turn the sailors into their own.

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:13.920
Then, our husbands were also...?

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:16.760
Please, could you change everyone back?!

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:18.260
Kitaro.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:20.470
Let's look into it.

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:21.970
Kitaro!

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:28.020
The fog...

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:30.610
Give me a ladle...

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:34.820
Give me a ladle...

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:38.370
Give me a ladle...

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:39.450
Dad.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:42.120
Right. Use it!

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:43.250
Okay!

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:44.710
Give me a ladle...

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:47.330
There! There's the ladle you wanted!

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:50.630
Give me a ladle...

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:58.550
It's almost sad to watch.

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:00.760
Oh!

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:08.730
Who's that?!

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:10.980
It's the Umizato!

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:13.070
UMIZATO

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:15.690
I've heard about it before.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:20.320
Long ago during the Edo period,
<i>kitamaebune</i> that passed through here

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:24.240
were sunk by him for their treasure.

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:27.710
So it's you, GeGeGe no Kitaro.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.840
You're the one impeding my minions!

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:33.250
Your minions?!

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.710
You mean these Funa-Yurei?!

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:37.470
That's right.

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:43.470
They're for pulling up the treasure
from the <i>kitamaebune</i> that are still sunk.

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:48.270
Kitaro...

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:57.570
Man, I walk the ocean until I'm exhausted
and I can't even find a single coin.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.110
No!

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:06.250
-Rat Man-san?!
-Ow, ow, ow...

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:08.000
M-Mana-chan?

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:12.830
In order to pull up all of the treasure
sunk below the ocean,

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:15.420
I can't have enough minions.

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:21.510
I'll need to turn more and more humans
into Funa-Yurei.

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:24.760
Do you think you can get away with that?!

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:29.390
I was finally freed
from being long sealed away.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:31.270
I won't let you interfere!

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:36.650
Could that be...?

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:52.420
Then, if we return those souls to
everyone's bodies, maybe...

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:56.170
No way! The shrine's door is really heavy!

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.710
It'll take more than a little tug to open!

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:03.090
What if everyone in this town
came together and pulled at once?

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:07.310
But...

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:09.180
To go up against a <i>yokai</i>...

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:11.690
We're just ordinary humans...

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:14.270
I...

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:16.940
I love this town.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:19.400
It has history.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:21.280
It has lots of nature.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:23.860
The food tastes so good.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:26.950
But, the biggest reason is

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:30.750
because everyone is so pleasant.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.370
They're so warm,

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:36.540
and so energetic.

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:43.050
My dad, and Uncle Shoji, and Aunt Rie,
and everyone!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:48.060
If everyone in Sakaiminato comes together
there's nothing we can't do!

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:49.220
I know it!

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:58.020
We can't have a cute girl like this
say all that and not do anything...

00:16:58.150 --> 00:16:58.980
Right?

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.230
Yeah.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:07.200
Let's rescue everyone
who's been turned into Funa-Yurei!

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:09.990
Yeah!

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.000
Kitaro!

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:24.840
Everyone in Sakaiminato is going to get
Uncle Shoji and the others' souls back!

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:27.930
<i>Try to at least be useful
at a time like this!</i>

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:29.510
Why do I--

00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:33.350
I'm going, I'm going! I'm going already!

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:38.150
What are you doing, Funa-Yurei?!

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:41.860
Force them into
becoming Funa-Yurei if you have to!

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:51.660
Aunt Rie!

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.250
<i>It's ready!</i>

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:54.410
Everyone!

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:57.620
Ready, go!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:07.720
Something's pulling us...!

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:13.810
Heave ho! Heave ho!

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:15.350
Hold on!

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:16.810
Stay strong, everyone!

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:21.980
Heave ho!

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:29.410
D-Dammit...!

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:31.780
Looks like we made it in time.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:39.210
Honestly, Rollo Cloth, you're so slow.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:40.920
I couldn't help it!

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:44.960
I had to carry
a buncha heavy folks like y'all at once!

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.470
-What?!
-Sorry

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:48.630
Could you keep it down?

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:52.100
My head's pounding from a hangover.

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:56.850
Wally Wall.

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:02.900
Hair Needles!

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:09.660
Everybody, ready...

00:19:10.070 --> 00:19:11.410
Go!

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:31.180
Curses!

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:34.850
This is all because you interfered!

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:46.360
Kitaro!

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:50.530
Uncle Shoji?!

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:51.910
Mana...?

00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:59.580
Dammit! What are they doing?

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:02.210
I could have made that throw in time!

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:04.590
Center fielder!

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:06.210
Throw home!

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:07.710
I've got this!

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:10.010
Leave it to Sniper Shoji!

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:25.560
Take this! Finger Guns!

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:40.290
Kitaro, you did it!

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:50.550
Recharge me!

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:50.550
73RD HARBOR FISHING FESTIVAL

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:59.560
It's a nice town like you said, Mana.

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:02.060
Isn't it, Cat-san?!

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:04.390
Here, <i>yokai</i>-san. Eat this.

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:05.270
This, too!

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:06.810
And this!

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:10.030
I'm already going to have to
put my diet on hold!

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:12.570
What do ya mean "already"?
Ya never started.

00:21:13.110 --> 00:21:15.700
Wally Wall.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:20.200
The reason that weak baseball club
made it through the Koshien series

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:23.370
was all thanks to me,
Sniper Shoji, and my--

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:27.670
U-Um, you know, you've already
repeated that story a hundred times...

00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:41.430
This all feels really nice, Dad.

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:43.560
Indeed.

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:53.110
I wish this moment
could last forever and ever...

